  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A thief wants to rob houses arranged in a line. Each house has some amount of money. The thief cannot rob two consecutive houses as it triggers an alarm. Find the maximum amount of money the thief can steal.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line contains a single integer NNN denoting the total number of houses\nSecond line contains NNN space-separated integers denoting the amount of money in each house\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nPrint a single integer representing the maximum amount of loot possible\n\nSubtasks\n\n1≤1 \\leq 1≤ nums.length ≤100 \\leq 100≤100\n0≤0 \\leq 0≤ nums[i] ≤400 \\leq 400≤400",
